// R11 gap 5 (docs/OWNERSHIP.md, "Still broken" table, row 5): reassigning an
// `arc` `var` leaks the previous box. `v = "two"` boxes the new literal
// (R11 retain rule 1, BOX) and overwrites `v`'s C-local storage; nothing
// drops the box `v` held a moment before, because the drop pass only ever
// schedules ONE release per binding id, at scope exit, and has no notion of
// "this place was reassigned N times before that." The same class of gap
// R16 documents for `owned` locals (a moved-from revival), applied to `arc`.
//
// This fixture ISOLATES that gap alone: `v` is declared once, outside any
// nested block, so the block-scoped-local gap
// (examples/leaks/block_scoped_local.cell) cannot also fire here, and the
// initial box and every reassignment are all plain string literals, never a
// struct field or a `shared` unbox. tools/check.sh's `leaks` stage pins the
// expected count; see that file for the number and the commit measured at.
//
// Status: parses, passes `cell check`. LLVM and MLIR refuse it (scalar-first,
// same as examples/arc.cell); this file lives under examples/leaks/ so it is
// invisible to the top-level examples/*.cell corpus, agreement, and
// mlir-lowering loops (see examples/leaks/README.md).

pub fn print_int(copy value: Int);

pub fn main() {
    var arc v = "one"
    var i = 0
    while i < 1000 {
        v = "two"
        i = i + 1
    }
    print_int(i)
}
